So here it is, my hard tried first wizard ascension:
Wiz-Elf-Mal-Cha, wishless, genocideless, poly*less
(in fact my first ascension of a non-fighter, the others were Val, Sam 
and Bar)

Having the previous ascensions all found an early wand of wishing, I 
wanted to try wishless this time; and it was quite astonishing how much 
nice pieces of an ascension kit are just lying around the dungeon...  I 
also did want to go genocideless as I did already the two ascensions 
before, I like it more to deal with purle h/L's than to simply genocide 
them... Feels quite like cheating (but yes, I do like conflict OTOH :D)
And for poly*less, I was never quite a fan of polyself/polypiling; I 
thought I would do polypiling for wishless, but as I found all I needed, 
I decided later to do also poly*less.

Being inspired by the discussion about protection-racket here some time 
ago, I tried this time to stay *really* behind my pet and make it down 
with as few hits of myself as possible; I did not want to do a full 
protection-run (as Wizards lack the money and I did not want to go 
treasure-hunting), but I just wanted to try leaving the pet fight after 
all my combat-characters before.  And it worked surprisingly well, 
although a hand full of wizards had to pay the attempt with their lives.

On the final run, I got really lucky and found a +3 elven mithril and +5 
orcish helm somewhere at the top of the mines; those surely helped a 
lot!  And as side-note, I kept the helm on all the way up to ascension.

Minetown-altar was cross-aligned, but I found a bag of holding somewhere 
in the mines and one of the stores had a magic marker.  Unfortunatelly, 
Sokoban was the bag of holding ending (I seem to always get it, had 
reflection only some two or three games in total I reached 
Sokoban-top!), so I did not finish it.

By the time I had finished Sokoban and the Mines up to Mine's End, I 
decided (with advice from you guys, thanks!) to switch my mithril 
against leather and start spell-casting instead of only fighting with 
daggers/Sting I had by then. The dungeon had an unattended altar, which 
I converted and got Magicbane; the first time ever I touched this 
mystical blade!

I found some more bones, one of a previous of my wizards, and one giving 
me a magic lamp!  This was really nice, as I had already used Sunsword 
instead of Excalibur once just for the light (I tend to never find magic 
lamps on my own; this was my first or second all through my 
nethack-experience so far).  The quest was fairly easy, the Dark One 
went down to a wand of cold I had found, just tried it...  With the Eye 
of the Aethiopica, the fun really starts!

I was still missing most spells, so I wrote a spellbook of create 
monster and tried sacrificing/praying for spellbooks.  But this bored me 
at some point, and I simply descended deeper; found spellbook of magic 
missile on Medusa's, then everything went quite smooth.  Found 
speedboots and jumping boots on the same dungeon level, and decided to 
go with speed as I had done before (but, maybe I'm going with jumping 
next time, it is probably quite nice for Astral after using a wand of 
teleport!).

In the castle armouries, I found a coruthaum; but I thought my orcish 
helm would be quite stylish and it saved me the enchant-armor-scrolls 
for it.  I had found four markers up to this point, and now wrote them 
all down to charging, enchant weapon for my daggers and Firebrand I had 
got as second sacrifice gift (I like the *brands), gold detection and 
enchant armor until everything was +4 or +5, giving me AC -42 with my 
divine protection.  (Ah, I had killed a silver dragon from a throne room 
some levels above, from this I had SDSM)  However, I realized I had 
forgotten to write spellbook of cure sickness when all markers were dry...

The valley wraiths together with some succubi brought me up to XL 30, 
and I couldn't believe my >700 Pw when I saw them...  Quite nice!  Also, 
the damage of magic missile was really, really astonishing!  With a 
bouncing magic missile, master- and arch-liches went down in two turns! 
  BTW, magic mapping is simply cool for Gehennom!

Near the bottom I finally found a fifth marker and wrote my cure 
sickness, just in case I needed it for Pestilence.

With cursed teleport and cursed gain level, the sanctum was done quite 
quickly; only the Wizard returned literally a few turns after I had 
killed him first:  I level-ported down to the vibrating square, did the 
invocation, went down, killed a master-lich appearing, went back up to 
level-port down into the sanctum, and there he was!  But well, it didn't 
cost more than 35 Pw for finger of death, and on my last ascension I did 
only kill him *twice* (that is, the first time and on earth), so I can't 
complain...

The run was quite smoothly, except what, on earth after killing the 
Wizard, I notice I had forgotten my scrolls of gold detection at my 
Sokoban stash (I did only re-read spellbooks and grabbed K-rations 
there)!  So well, I did all the planes with the amulet around my neck 
and secret door detection when it felt warm...  It was possible, but a 
bit tiring; however, with the amulet, spellcasting becomes quite 
expensive...  I tried to save as much energy as possible (and because of 
conflict throughout the Endgame I indead didn't need much spells), but 
some times I got low on power.

Finally on Astral, I switched nearly entirely to my saved wands instead 
of spellcasting; only for two arch-liches attacking me together I used 
magic missile, but they went down easily.  First I tried Famine, wrong 
altar; before this ascension, I two times found the right altar on first 
try and once used a helm of opposite alignment which I didn't have here. 
  So learn how to go back...

I meat Pestilence on the way back (don't know how this happened, I had 
planned to do it last), but my wand of death made quick work of it; I 
tried its altar, and it was also wrong.  Finally I made it to Death, 
magic missile killed him, but then I tried to teleport away some 
priests/angels and got him revived immediatelly after killing him... 
Well, killed him the second time, and now everything was ready to reach 
my altar finally.

domob, chaotic male elven Wizard




